{
  "_doc": "Your own cars (cars/build_cars.sh). Per car: source model, which objects are the wheels and the steering wheel, and the vehicle's specs. forward = the model's axis the car's nose points along. Lengths in metres, mass in kg. / \u81ea\u4f5c\u8eca\u4e21\u306e\u8a2d\u5b9a glass = window material names made invisible (make_glass.py); glass_objects = objects given their own window material first (when windows or lamp lenses share a material with something else). blinkers = indicator lens/bulb faces given <Name>_BlinkerL/_BlinkerR (side from CARLA y) and made to blink by make_lights.py; mirrors = side-mirror glass faces given <Name>_MirrorGlass (a mirror material). Rule keys: name/objects/materials, material, per_face, box {x|y|abs_y|z: [lo, hi]} in the vehicle frame (metres, x forward from mid-axle, y right, z up from the ground), tint, side (car_guide ch. 4, 12). lenses = lamp lens faces that come out opaque in UE, made invisible with the glass (<Name>_LensGlass). rhd_convert = make a left-hand-drive model right-hand drive: move (shared parts: wheel, column, cluster, pedals, as one block, axis_y), mirror (driver-shaped mouldings, per_face box symmetric about the centre line), flip_uv / unmirror (graphics on mirrored faces read right again; uv_box picks a decal in an atlas) (car_guide ch. 13). drop = helper meshes removed; split = one mesh cut per material and connected piece; vertex_colour_base = game-rip vertex colours and atlas UVs made visible in UE; steering_wheel box/in = the wheel cut out of merged meshes by a CAR-frame box, exclude = parts never joined to the wheel. Heavy NPC vehicles (car_guide ch. 16): steering_wheel {\"none\": true} (no interior, needs driver_eye), npc_only (never parked, random traffic or a hero choice; own_cars.py), base_type, brake_torque_nm / handbrake_torque_nm (per wheel), collision_box {x,y,z: [lo, hi]} (own physics body box), com_height_m, max_texture, wheel_radius_m (dry-run radius for drivetrain.py).",
